---
import Policy from '../components/Policy.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
export const prerender = false;
---
<Policy title="Privacy" updated="October 6, 2026" description="What Granthalaya keeps about you, who can see it, and how to take it with you or delete it.">
  <p class="lead">Granthalaya keeps only what it needs to give you a shelf. It has no ads, no tracking scripts and sells nothing.</p>

  <h2>What we keep</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>From Google, when you sign in:</b> your name, email address and profile photo. Your email is never shown to anyone.</li>
    <li><b>What you add:</b> the things on your shelf, their status, ratings, dates and reviews, the comments and likes you leave on reviews, collections, and your profile (username, bio, links and favourites). Lines you saved before reviews replaced them are kept too.</li>
    <li><b>Safety records:</b> people you block, and reports you send.</li>
    <li><b>Technical records:</b> the companies that run the site keep short-lived server logs (like your IP address and browser) to keep it working and secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who can see it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, username and photo are visible to everyone, even on a private account, so people can find and block you.</li>
    <li>With a public account, your shelf, reviews, collections and stats are visible to anyone, except entries you mark <b>Only me</b>. Your reviews also show on each title’s page.</li>
    <li>With a private account, only you can see your shelf, reviews, collections and stats. Comments and likes you leave on someone else’s public review stay public, even from a private account.</li>
    <li>Likes and comments on a review are seen by whoever can see that review. A comment you leave shows with your name, even if your account is private.</li>
    <li>If you block someone, neither of you can see the other’s profile.</li>
    <li>Your shelf appears on the welcome page for new visitors only if you turn on <b>Feature my shelf</b>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who helps run the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Supabase</b> stores the database, on servers in Mumbai, India, and handles signing in.</li>
    <li><b>Vercel</b> hosts the website.</li>
    <li><b>Google</b> confirms who you are when you sign in.</li>
    <li><b>Cloudflare Turnstile</b> runs a quick check that a person, not a bot, is creating a new shelf.</li>
    <li><b>Open Library, Google Books, TMDB, Wikipedia, Google Gemini and Groq</b> help look up titles, covers and short facts about them. Our server sends them only what’s being looked up (a title, or what you typed in search), never anything about you.</li>
    <li><b>Posters, covers, photos and streaming logos</b> load straight from TMDB, Open Library and Google Books, so those services see your browser’s request for the image, as with any picture on the web. Covers from the bookshops Akshardhara and BookGanga do not: our server fetches them and passes them on, so those shops never see your browser.</li>
    <li><b>Akshardhara and BookGanga</b> are Indian bookshops that let us show some of their books and covers. Our server reads their public book lists. Nothing about you is sent to them, unless you follow a “Buy at” link to their site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>One cookie keeps you signed in for up to 90 days on a device. Your choice of light or dark lives in your browser. There are no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Change anything on your profile or shelf at any time.</li>
    <li>Make your account private, or mark single entries <b>Only me</b>.</li>
    <li><b>Download your data</b> in Settings: everything you’ve added, as spreadsheets in a zip file you keep.</li>
    <li><b>Delete your account</b> in Settings. Your profile, shelf, reviews, comments, likes and collections are removed right away. Copies can stay in the database provider’s backups for a short time before they’re gone too.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>You need to be 18 or older to make a shelf.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>To ask about your data, {site.contact ? <>email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact}`}>{site.contact}</a></> : 'use the options in Settings, or report it from any profile'}. If this policy changes in a way that matters, the site will say so before it takes effect.</p>
</Policy>
